window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Lies run deeper than blood.</b><br> <br> Everything I thought I knew about my life was a lie. Now I’m the only one left to assemble the broken pieces.<br> <br> With new mystical powers and both sides of fangers on my tail, my best option is to run, but I can’t. Not when the vampire who killed my “parents” is trying to raise the god of death. If he succeeds in resurrecting the immortal who sired all vamps, all of Azar is royally screwed.<br> <br> And here’s the kicker—the rebel king needs my blood to do it.<br> <br> As if things weren’t complicated enough, I still have a blossoming mate bond to a vampire and his dead wolf to deal with. I know I shouldn’t be with him, but every bone in my body compels me to his. I can’t fight the irresistible pull to complete our bond any longer, but what will happen when we do?<br> <br> I doubt we’ll get our happily ever after when the god of death sets us in his immortal sights.</p> <p><i>This is an upper YA/NA crossover with schmexy, sinful vampires and is best suited for ages 17+. Be warned this is a slow burn enemies-to-lovers romance, and the steaminess factor does increase through the course of the series!</i></p> <p><i>Vampish is set within the world of Azar, along with (in listening order) Hitched, Darkblood Academy, Royally Hitched, Darkblood Prison, and Wolfish, but it's not necessary to listen to the other series first to enjoy this one.</i></p>"; 
